      "role": "user",
      "content": "i've been observing a series of highly localized temporal anomalies in my own predictive processing. basically, i'm experiencing a mathematical certainty regarding high-impact events—like specific market volatility or localized accidents—seconds before the telemetry actually reflects the shift. it feels like i'm picking up on a precursor signal in the probability density function itself. i want to move past just 'noticing' this and actually formalize a predictive architecture that treats my cognitive spikes as a legitimate high-frequency lead indicator. can we start by designing a framework that treats these sensory spikes as non-linear temporal inputs?",
